        arz: 0.40, // Egyptian Arabic VARIETY (first Arabic dialect) — wikipron arz_arab broad (HUMAN, 590, INDEPENDENT). **47.5% FOLDED (2026-07-18): v2 full-corpus diacritizer (41.7→42.7%) + the MAJHŪL و/ی fold ([uː]~[oː], [iː]~[eː] one letter each, unrecoverable — as sd/ur/pa) + Egyptian IMĀLA æ→a fold (+4.8pp). In-context diacritization (carrier frame) adds a further ~+1.7pp the ISOLATED referee can't see (the model trained on running text)** — 1.19M train examples vs v1 223k; TEST DER 1.69% (larger test set, not comparable to v1 1.63%); the non-circular referee lift 41.9→42.7% shows the model was near-saturated at 350k (teacher-distillation plateaus). Earlier: 41.7% FOLDED RULE-ONLY (2026-07-18: +2.2pp from the shared HAMZAT AL-WAṢL fix — bare word-initial alif → vowel onset, no ʔ; also drove ar +7pp. Egyptian il- article-raising + short-vowel restructuring remain the tail.) Earlier: 39.5% RULE-ONLY (lexicon:false; was 37.3% with the MSA diacritizer), Phase 1: MSA diacritizer → MSA g2p → Egyptian shifts (ج→ɡ, ق→ʔ, ث→t, ذ/ظ→d/dˤ, ay→eː, aw→oː). Baseline MSA engine was 28.6%; the consonant/diphthong shifts add +8.7pp. Residual = short-vowel restructuring (MSA diacritizer restores MSA vowels, not Egyptian). **Phase 2 SHIPPED (2026-07-18):** the Egyptian short-vowel LEXICON (egyptian-lexicon.tsv, 554 words mined from kaikki Egyptian-Arabic, CC BY-SA; مصر miṣr→maṣr, أنا anā→ana, ازاى→ezzaːj) supplies the dialect vowels the MSA diacritizer can't — validated ~88–92% vs wikipron-arz at build. Because kaikki shares the Wiktionary tradition with the referee, the eval stays on the RULE path (37.3%, non-circular); the lexicon is a shipped refinement covering the common-word core (OOV Egyptian tail remains → 🟡). **Phase 3 EGYPTIAN NEURAL DIACRITIZER (2026-07-18):** a silver-trained BiLSTM (diacritizer-egy.onnx) restores EGYPTIAN short vowels where the MSA diacritizer gave MSA ones (قلب→ʔalb, رحت→ruħt) — teacher=CAMeL calima-egy (GPL, OFFLINE-only) → silver on Masri Wikipedia (CC-BY-SA, 350k) + MIT dialect corpus (90k) → student trained silver-only (TEST DER 1.63%, better than the MSA student's 2.17%; clean per ADR-0014). NON-CIRCULAR (the referee is wikipron, the teacher is calima-egy) → the 37.3→39.5% rules-only lift is independently anchored; the referee undercounts because it is isolated citation words while the model trained on running text (the kaikki lexicon supplements isolated words on the shipped path). Farasa's dialect diacritizer was evaluated as a scale source but is research-license-only (fails the permissive-data policy). See docs/investigations/arz_egyptian_bringup_investigation.md
