        be: 0.95, // Belarusian / беларуская (be) — East Slavic, Cyrillic. Rule g2p mirroring Ukrainian's iotated/palatalisation machinery. wikipron bel_cyrl_narrow (HUMAN, 7259): 97.2% FOLDED. Belarusian orthography is PHONETIC — akanne (unstressed о→а, е→я) is SPELLED, so ⟨о⟩ is only ever stressed → [o] and NO stress dict is needed. Signatures: ⟨г⟩→ɣ (velar fricative), RETROFLEX hushers ж/ш/ч→ʐ/ʂ/t͡ʂ (+ дж→d͡ʐ, дз→d͡z), the unique ⟨ў⟩→u̯ (post-vocalic)/w, ⟨і⟩ IOTATED (Іван→jivan, unlike Ukrainian), ⟨э⟩→ɛ vs soft ⟨е⟩→(j)e, dark ⟨л⟩→ɫ, PALATALISATION before ь/і/iotated, and — unlike Ukrainian — regressive VOICING assimilation + word-final devoicing (горад→ɣorat, хлеб→xlʲep, снег→sʲnʲex). REGRESSIVE PALATALISATION was the iterative lever (90.9%→97.2%): a SIBILANT/affricate с/з/ц/дз softens before a palatalised coronal OR labial (везці→vʲesʲt͡sʲi, Зміцер→zʲmʲit͡sʲer) but NOT before a palatalised velar (-скі keeps hard с: Заборскі→zaborskʲi); ⟨т д н⟩ excluded as targets (referee-inconsistent: Пенсільванія keeps hard н) EXCEPT н→nʲ before a palatalised affricate (Аргенціна→arɣʲenʲt͡sʲina); + affricate/лл gemination. NO folds needed (narrow referee, clean). Residual is the loanword г→[ɡ] tail (46 rows: Ghana/Riga/Singapore, foreign names keep [ɡ]) + rare cluster assimilations. 🔷 single-source (wikipron bel, Wiktionary-derived). See docs/investigations/be_native_bringup_investigation.md
