        hu: 0.89, // Hungarian (magyar, Uralic) — wikipron hun_latn NARROW (PRIMARY, HUMAN, 64286) measured 92.6%; epitran hun-Latn (2nd, INDEPENDENT, 87.6%). Regular longest-match g2p: digraphs + geminate digraphs (ssz→sː, ggy→ɟː), ⟨s⟩→ʃ/⟨sz⟩→s (reversed), ⟨gy⟩→ɟ/⟨ty⟩→c, ⟨a⟩→ɒ, full long/short vowels, fixed first-syllable stress. Plus REGRESSIVE voicing assimilation (biztat→bistɒt — +12.5pp; epitran is NAIVE on it, hence its lower 2nd number), j-palatalization (feddj→fɛɟː), n→ŋ before k/ɡ. Folds: h~ɦ (intervocalic voicing), the hiatus j-glide (biblia→biblijɒ). Residual = szs→ʃː sibilant assimilation, final-h drop, proper nouns. See docs/investigations/hu_native_bringup_investigation.md
