        el: 0.89, // Modern Greek (Hellenic, Greek script) — wikipron ell_grek (PRIMARY, HUMAN, 19108) measured 91.1%; kaikki Greek (2nd, HUMAN, 19721) 90.0%. A CONTEXT-SENSITIVE scan (not a table map): the historical spellings collapse to /a e i o u/; VELAR PALATALISATION before front vowels (κ→c, γ→ʝ, χ→ç; γ-nasals γγ/γκ→ŋɡ/ŋɟ, initial γκ→ɡ); ⟨μπ ντ⟩ initial→b/d, MEDIAL→prenasalised mb/nd (before a vowel; before a consonant = μ+π/ν+τ); ⟨τσ τζ⟩→t͡s d͡z; ⟨αυ ευ⟩→a/e+[v/f] and ⟨σ⟩→[z] by the following voicing; double consonants simplify. SYNIZESIS applied only in the RELIABLE subset (unstressed [i] before a STRESSED vowel: κοιλιά→ciʎa, Λειβαδιά→livaðʝa) — the mixed γ/λ/ν middle is lexical → a 422-word CROSS-SOURCE-CONSENSUS (wikipron∩kaikki) synizesis lexicon on the SHIPPED path lifts phonemizeWord to 93.2%/92.2% (eval uses phonemizeWordRules → the 91.1% above is non-circular). Stress not emitted (referees don't mark it; tonos tracked only for synizesis). Folds: kaikki dots, rhotic ɾ~r. → 🟡 reliable + LEXICAL-TAIL. Residual (~10%) = lexical synizesis (Κύριος keeps [i] but κοιλιά synizes — register-conditioned, needs a lexicon) + variable medial prenasalisation + loan/proper-noun tail. Two same-tradition (Wiktionary) human referees, both ~90%. Numbers/stress deferred. See docs/investigations/el_native_bringup_investigation.md
        nya: 0.97, // Chichewa / Chinyanja (Bantu N31, Malawi/Zambia/Mozambique, Latin) — wikipron nya_latn (PRIMARY, HUMAN, narrow, 1562) measured 99.4%; kaikki nya (2nd, HUMAN, 1526) 98.2%; epitran nya-Latn (3rd, INDEPENDENT, broad) 92.7%. THREE referees, real triangulation → ✅. A pure greedy longest-match g2p (open CV). Signatures (narrow Wiktionary convention): IMPLOSIVES ⟨b d⟩→ɓ ɗ (plain after a nasal: ⟨mb⟩→ᵐb, ⟨nd⟩→ⁿd), the single LIQUID ⟨l⟩=⟨r⟩→ɽ, PRENASALISED ⟨mb nd ng nj⟩→ᵐb ⁿd ᵑɡ ⁿd͡ʒ (⟨ng'⟩→ŋ), aspirates ⟨ph th kh tch⟩→pʰ tʰ kʰ t͡ʃʰ, and the prenasalised/labialised aspirate CLUSTERS ⟨nth mph nkh ntch nkhw thw⟩→ⁿtʰ ᵐpʰ ᵑkʰ ⁿt͡ʃʰ ᵑkʷʰ tʷʰ, ⟨Cy⟩ palatalisation→Cʲ, and the WHISTLED clusters ⟨ps bz⟩→psʲ bzʲ (both human referees). Folds: tone/stress (backbone, tone unwritten→DEFERRED), labialisation ʷ~w, palatalisation ʲ~j, implosive ɓ~b/ɗ~d + prenasal superscript→full (for the broad epitran), kaikki syllable dots. Residual (~1.3%) = proper-noun/loanword tail (place-name final vowels, Mozambique/Marx). Tone + noun-class number concord deferred. See docs/investigations/nya_native_bringup_investigation.md
