        ilo: 0.80, // Ilocano / Iloko (ilo) — Austronesian (Northern Luzon, NOT Bisayan; ~8M, lingua franca of the north). Latin, near-phonemic. Rule g2p with the Ilocano-distinctive HIATUS: a HIGH vowel ⟨i u⟩ before a vowel GLIDES (dua→dwa, radio→ɾadjo, dies→djɛs) — unlike Bisayan's uniform glottal — while non-high hiatus keeps the glottal (tao→taʔo). Signature 6th vowel ⟨e⟩→[ɯ]~[ɛ] (folded). ⟨ll⟩=native geminate (not Spanish lj). THREE referees: wikipron ilo_latn (PRIMARY, 926, proper-noun-heavy) 82.7% + kaikki ilo (973, native) 84.5% + epitran ilo-Latn (887) 75.9%. Folds: stress, the 6th vowel ɯ~ɛ~e, ng-ambiguity ŋ~nɡ~ŋɡ, word-final+initial glottal, ɾ~r. 🟡 bounded — the ceiling is the orthography-AMBIGUOUS gliding/hiatus (high vowel glides vs stays syllabic is stress/lexeme-dependent, not spelling-predictable → needs a stress model/lexicon), inflated harder by the Spanish-proper-noun referee. Numbers deferred. See docs/investigations/ilo_native_bringup_investigation.md
