        hil: 0.92, // Hiligaynon / Ilonggo (hil) — Austronesian (Western Bisayan, ~9M), Latin, near-phonemic. Rule g2p mirroring the sibling Cebuano (⟨ng⟩→ŋ, word-initial + hiatus glottal, penultimate stress) + the SPANISH-LOAN deltas ⟨j⟩→[h] (Bermejo→beɾmeho) and ⟨f⟩→[p] (Fuentes→puentes, Demafeliz→demapelis). TWO independent HUMAN referees: wikipron hil_latn (PRIMARY, proper-noun-heavy, 465) 94.4% FOLDED + kaikki hil (SECONDARY, native vocab, 477) 94.1%. Folds: stress (unwritten penult), the unwritten word-final glottal (mango→maŋoʔ, lexical→deferred), ɾ~r, ɲ~nj, the 3-vowel lax allophones o~ɔ/e~ɛ/u~ʊ/i~ɪ, inconsistent word-initial ʔ. Residual = Spanish rising diphthongs ⟨ue/ie⟩→[we/je] (origin-ambiguous from spelling; native hiatus rule gives [uʔe]) + hiatus-glottal variation. Numbers deferred. 🟢 bounded (two human referees ~94%). See docs/investigations/hil_native_bringup_investigation.md
        ckb: 0.92, // Central Kurdish / Sorani (ckb) — Iranian (NW), the SORANI Perso-Arabic alphabet. Complements the Latin-script Kurmanji `kmr`. Native left-to-right greedy scan. TWO independent HUMAN referees: wikipron ckb_arab_broad (PRIMARY, 972) 94.9% FOLDED + kaikki ckb (SECONDARY, 1037) 94.2%. (epitran ckb-Arab exists but diverges ~25% → unusable, not used.) Sorani is a near-FULL alphabet (writes all LONG vowels ا→aː ێ→eː ۆ→oː وو→uː ی→iː + the short /a/ ە) — UNLIKE the Arabic/Persian abjads. The ONE fold = the UNWRITTEN short /ɪ/ (bizroke): epenthetic in clusters, not positionally predictable (my crude epenthesis scored 71% < the fold), so folded (the abjad short-vowel wall but only ONE vowel). Signatures: pharyngeals ح→ħ ع→ʕ, velarised ڵ→ɫ vs ل→l, trill ڕ→r vs tap ر→ɾ, ئ→ʔ glottal onset, و/ی matres (glide next to a vowel else the vowel). Length + the glide~high-vowel matres folded (house backbone strips length). Numbers deferred (dialect-variable orthography). 🟡 bounded by the unwritten short-i. See docs/investigations/ckb_native_bringup_investigation.md
        bg: 0.98, // Bulgarian / български (bg) — South Slavic, Cyrillic, "clean" (highly phonemic). Native left-to-right g2p + phonotactic post-rules. TWO independent HUMAN referees: wikipron bul_cyrl_narrow (PRIMARY, 46034) 99.6% FOLDED + kaikki bg (SECONDARY, 47616) 99.5%. Rules: PALATALISATION (only before ь я ю, NOT и/е — cleaner than Russian), DARK-L (л→l before front V, lʲ before ь/я/ю, ɫ elsewhere), н→ŋ before к/ɡ, FINAL DEVOICING, REGRESSIVE VOICING assim (/v/ voicing-transparent as [v]), SIBILANT assim (с/з→ʃ before ʃ/t͡ʃ), стк→ск + stop-geminate collapse. The ONE systematic fold = VOWEL REDUCTION (unstressed {a,ɤ}→[ɐ], {ɔ,u}→[o]) — stress-conditioned + unwritten, so we emit full phonemic vowels and fold the two reduction classes (akanye treatment). Numbers compose with the и connector (21→dvajsɛt i ɛdnɔ). Floor 0.98 (near-ceiling, dual-referee). ✅ reliable — the strongest bring-up of the batch (two large human referees both ≥99.5%). See docs/investigations/bg_native_bringup_investigation.md
        ti: 0.88, // Tigrinya / ትግርኛ (ti) — North Ethiosemitic (~9M, Eritrea + Tigray), the Ge'ez/Fidäl SYLLABARY-abugida, read by the SHARED Ge'ez engine (core/geez.ts, same fidel→CV lookup + epenthetic-ɨ deletion as Amharic `am`). kaikki tir (PRIMARY, HUMAN, 26) measured 96.2% FOLDED; epitran tir-Ethi (an INDEPENDENT rule-based impl, 898) corroborates at 94.3%. SIGNATURE = the PRESERVED SEMITIC GUTTURALS that Amharic merged away: ⟨ሐ ኀ⟩→ħ, ⟨ዐ⟩→ʕ (the pharyngeals), ⟨አ⟩→ʔ, ⟨ኸ⟩→x; the guttural 1st-order vowel stays central [ə] (kaikki ʔɐf, ʔɐdɾi). ⟨ቀ⟩→kʼ (human referee's value; epitran uses q — folded). Fidel table adapted from the Amharic one (306 rows) with the guttural restoration. UNWRITTEN (shared): GEMINATION (folded) + the epenthetic 6th-order ɨ (folded vs epitran, which keeps all). Units 1-10 attested in kaikki → verified numbers. Floor at 0.88 = one-word margin on the thin 26-word human referee. 🔷 single-source (thin human anchor + a rule-based large corroborator). See docs/investigations/ti_native_bringup_investigation.md
        syl: 0.76, // Sylheti / ꠍꠤꠟꠐꠤ ꠘꠣꠉꠞꠤ (syl) — Eastern Indo-Aryan (Bengali-Assamese), the SYLOTI NAGRI abugida (~11M). wikipron syl_sylo_broad (PRIMARY, HUMAN, 397, Syloti Nagri) measured 78.1% FOLDED; kaikki Sylheti (2nd human, Syloti Nagri) corroborates. SCOPE PASSES (Syloti Nagri is a real Sylheti script with a puthi literature + Unicode + Wiktionary usage — the bho/awa pattern, NOT the ctg no-standard case). Read by the generic abugida engine (inherent ɔ, Bengali-style final+medial inherent deletion). SIGNATURE = SPIRANTISATION (the split from Bengali, DERIVED from wikipron): ꠇ/ꠈ→x, ꠌ/ꠍ→s, ꠎ/ꠏ→z, ꠙ→ɸ, ꠚ→f, ꠡ→ʃ, ꠢ→ɦ, aspiration lost on voiced stops; ꠋ anusvara→ŋ, ꠂ dvisvara→i diphthong. TONE (H/L, from lost breathy voice) is UNWRITTEN → deferred (acute folded). Folds: tone (acute), tie-bar, geminate CC~Cː, r~ɾ, a~ɑ, dental n̪, u~ʊ. Residual = context-sensitive spirantisation (geminate ꠌꠍ keeps t͡ʃ), hiatus glide (ia~ija, variable), lexical ꠇ→x~k. Numbers deferred. 🔷 single-source (one human referee family). See docs/investigations/syl_native_bringup_investigation.md
        ug: 0.97, // Uyghur / ئۇيغۇرچە (ug) — Turkic (Karluk), Xinjiang (~11M), the UYGHUR ARABIC alphabet. wikipron uig_arab_broad (PRIMARY, HUMAN, 2673) measured 98.2% FOLDED — near-ceiling. The Uyghur Arabic script is a FULL PHONEMIC ALPHABET (writes all 8 vowels), so NO short-vowel restoration (unlike the Arabic/Persian/Urdu abjads) — a plain greedy letter→IPA scan + one code rule. Signatures: 8 vowels ا→ɑ (BACK a), ە→ɛ, ې→e, ى→i, و→o, ۆ→ø, ۇ→u, ۈ→y (harmony is WRITTEN); the hamza ئ→ʔ (glottal onset before word-initial/hiatus vowels); ⟨چ ج⟩→t͡ʃ d͡ʒ, ⟨غ⟩→ʁ, ⟨خ⟩→χ, ⟨ق⟩→q, ⟨ڭ⟩→ŋ; ⟨ف⟩→[p] (Uyghur nativises /f/); word-final STOP devoicing (b/d/g→p/t/k, but z/ʒ/ʁ/d͡ʒ stay voiced). Fold: tie-bar. Residual = isolated alphabet-letter entries (ئا→ʔɑ vs a). Non-tonal. epitran uig-Arab independently corroborates the consonant map (cruder on vowels: a not ɑ, drops the glottal). Numbers deferred. See docs/investigations/ug_native_bringup_investigation.md
